H:Cr3.1.6c, a guide look-for on the showing: the plan run, with the element changed after the tech rehearsal named on the cue sheet; TH:Re9.1.6b, a written item: one production element of an unseen described production and the aesthetic choice it shows; TH:Re9.1.6a, a written item: a judgment of the teacher's unseen scene with two pieces of evidence and one criterion from the class card; TH:Re9.1.6c, a written item: who the described production is for and how its aim appeals to them. Each item is marked met, partly or not yet. Out: several elements weighed together (grade 7), the real venue (grade 8). Tools: cue sheet, design sketch sheet and criteria card, Curio Class's own; a cue-calling practice tool or its printed cue cards. Free path: the room's light switch and blinds, voice and found-object sound, cardboard. Once-a-week path: 6 sessions | After unit 2 because design fixes a problem in a scene already staged and marked; judging grows from unit 1's written reaction and needs the criteria the class sets here. Before unit 4 because the devised piece uses a designed cue and the class criteria. The prop-sketch, cue-sheet, criteria-card and reason-because models start here | Candidate: a design maker from Africa or Asia, described and linked, beside the two | Hazards and controls: flashlights LED only, screw-closed battery doors, no coin or button batteries; no light into eyes and no flashing; nothing hung above heads, no ladders, no standing on chairs; scissors, card and tape; any blade cut by an adult; no heat or hot glue; a device's cable taped down. Bread and Puppet's pageants carry political messages: the unit studies their materials and scale only. Agent reads: sensitivity; safety (hands-on). |
