docs/courses/theater-grades-9-to-12/frame.md:297:| 19 | Level 4 | The student as critic. *What does a researched critique of a play I choose show me about my own work?* | 22 | th-g12-criticism | None | Responding (Re7, Re8, Re9). Works: a play of the student's choosing (read, seen live or in a lawful recording the school has), range-checked; unit 14's Sovereignty critique revisited as a model | Retrieval in day 2: unit 13's critique and unit 14's researched critique (th-g11-notice, th-g11-judge). Level 4 claims no id: TH:Re7.1.IIIa (owned in unit 13) in a response organized by history and culture; TH:Re8.1.IIIa (owned in unit 13) in proof and standards used to revise the student's own work; TH:Re8.1.IIIc (owned in unit 13) in tastes stated as grounds for research; TH:Re9.1.IIIa (owned in unit 14) in research backing or challenging choices; TH:Re9.1.IIIc (owned in unit 14) in a debated tie to current issues. Words: critique, standard, fairness, revise, issue, evidence. Showing: the critique read or recorded for the class. End-of-unit evidence, id by id: each id a look-for on the written or recorded critique with sources, or on the revision note on the student's own role or concept. Short path: 11 days | After the role so the critique can revise the student's own performance; before the production, which it improves | Candidate: a list of plays across regions offered for students who want one | A self-chosen play is checked by the teacher against the values rule and the sensitivity agent's read of the unit's list. Agent reads: sensitivity; safety (hands-on). |
